%% P2 p.2 asynchronous communication: a flight is completed on instance 1 and every other party learns it through the broker
sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Client (ATCC)
    participant I1 as instance1
    participant DB1 as PostgreSQL 1
    participant B as RabbitMQ (aisafe.events)
    participant I2 as instance2
    participant AM as Aircraft & Maintenance

    C->>I1: PATCH /api/scheduled-flights/{n}/complete
    I1->>DB1: one transaction: flight COMPLETED (revision n+1)<br/>+ event_outbox row "flight.completed"
    Note over I1: after the commit: own read model updated<br/>(read your own write)
    I1-->>C: 200 COMPLETED
    I1->>B: EventRelay: publish flight.completed (persistent)
    B-->>I1: publisher confirm
    I1->>DB1: delete the outbox row
    par fan-out: one copy per queue
        B->>I2: flight.events.instance2
        Note over I2: newer revision: read model updated<br/>(milliseconds after the commit)
        I2-->>B: ack after processing
    and
        B->>AM: aircraft.events.<instance>
        Note over AM: eventId not seen before:<br/>adds durationHours to the aircraft
        AM-->>B: ack after processing
    and
        B->>I1: flight.events.instance1 (its own event)
        Note over I1: already projected: skipped
        I1-->>B: ack
    end
